  "existingDescription": "An icon-only button with three emphasis levels, two sizes and four interaction states, built as a 24-variant component set. The icon itself is swappable from a library of 576 icons.\n\nPURPOSE: Triggers a single action where an icon alone carries the meaning, such as close, edit or favourite. Primary gives a filled brand treatment, Neutral a secondary surface with a visible border, and Subtle a quieter option for dense toolbars and table rows.\n\nBEHAVIOUR: Each variant and size pair ships Default, Hover, Disabled and Focus artwork. Hover swaps the background token (Background/Brand/Hover for Primary, Background/Default/Secondary Hover and Background/Default/Default Hover for the other two). Disabled uses Background/Disabled/Default, Border/Disabled/default and Icon/Disabled/On Disabled together, so the whole button dims as one. Focus is drawn with Stroke/Focus Ring. There is no pressed or loading state in the set.\n\nCOMPOSITION: Every variant wraps a single nested instance named \"container\", which holds one \"Icon\" vector. The container is shared across all 24 variants, so it carries the padding, border and background. AI code generators should look for an existing container or button-base component in the development codebase before writing a new wrapper.\n\nUSAGE: Use when space is tight and the action is well understood, or when the same action repeats many times in a list. Use the standard text button when the action needs a label. Pick Primary for the single main action in a view, Neutral for ordinary toolbar actions, and Subtle inside cards, tables and headers where a filled button would compete with content.\n\nCODE GENERATION NOTES: The component has no text layer, so the accessible name has to come from code. Always set an aria-label or equivalent, and a tooltip on hover and focus. Map Variant to a style prop, Size to Medium and Small only, and State to CSS pseudo-classes rather than separate components, since Hover and Focus are presentation only. Render Disabled with the disabled attribute and keep the element focusable if the reason needs explaining. Spacing comes from Space/300, Space/200 and Scale 07; borders from Stroke/Border and Scale 06. Icon/Danger/Tertiary appears in the token set, so check whether a destructive treatment is expected before hard-coding icon colour.",
